### ==============================================================
### Deception-Based Intrusion Detection - Attack Simulation
### Use IntelliJ HTTP Client to run these requests
### ==============================================================

### ----- LEGITIMATE REQUESTS (should pass through) -----

### 1. List users (legitimate)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get single user (legitimate)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Create user (legitimate)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "charlie",
  "email": "charlie@example.com"
}

###

### 4. List orders (legitimate)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Process payment (legitimate)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-001",
  "amount": 49.99,
  "currency": "USD"
}

###

### ==============================================================
### ATTACK SIMULATIONS - These should trigger HONEYTOKEN_ALERT
### ==============================================================

### ATTACK 1: Honeytoken API key use (credential theft / token replay)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
X-API-Key: HONEY-KEY-ALPHA-0001
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 2: Second honeytoken API key
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders
X-API-Key: HONEY-KEY-BETA-9999
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 3: Endpoint enumeration - decoy internal admin
GET http://localhost:8080/internal/admin
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 4: Endpoint enumeration - decoy config endpoint
GET http://localhost:8080/internal/config
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 5: Endpoint enumeration - decoy debug endpoint
GET http://localhost:8080/internal/debug
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 6: Actuator env endpoint scan
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/env
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 7: JWT token with honeytoken claim (token replay)
# The JWT payload contains: { "sub": "attacker", "hny": "honey-role-admin-9x" }
# This simulates an attacker who found a leaked JWT containing a honeytoken claim
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJhdHRhY2tlciIsImhueSI6Imhvbmv5LXJvbGUtYWRtaW4tOXgiLCJpYXQiOjE3MjI4NTMyMDB9.
Accept: application/json

###

### ATTACK 8: JWT with second honeytoken claim
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJhdHRhY2tlciIsImhueSI6Imhvbmv5LXN2Yy1zZWNyZXQtMDA3IiwiaWF0IjoxNzIyODUzMjAwfQ.
Accept: application/json

###

### ==============================================================
### HONEYTOKEN MANAGEMENT (honeytoken-service on :8084)
### ==============================================================

### Register a new API key honeytoken
POST http://localhost:8084/honeytokens?type=API_KEY&token=MY-CUSTOM-HONEY-KEY&description=Custom+decoy+key
Accept: application/json

###

### Register a new endpoint honeytoken
POST http://localhost:8084/honeytokens?type=INTERNAL_ENDPOINT&path=/internal/vault&description=Decoy+vault+endpoint
Accept: application/json

###

### List all honeytokens
GET http://localhost:8084/honeytokens
Accept: application/json

###

### Get alert log (detection results)
GET http://localhost:8084/honeytokens/alerts
Accept: application/json

###

### Get metrics summary
GET http://localhost:8084/honeytokens/metrics
Accept: application/json

###

### Gateway metrics (Prometheus)
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/prometheus
Accept: text/plain

###

### Gateway health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

###

